# Rendered by paisans. Do not edit: `paisans apply` overwrites this file.
#
# Routing for gate, imported by the gateway's block for
# gate.example.org. This is the one hostname the identity provider's callback
# is registered against, and it is NOT gated itself: gating the gate is a
# redirect loop. Its whole surface is oauth2-proxy's own -
# /oauth2/start, /oauth2/callback, /oauth2/sign_out, and the /oauth2/auth
# endpoint that this kind's own gate_provisional and gate_member snippets
# forward-auth to (see caddy.snippet.gates.tmpl) - so it proxies straight to
# `provisional`, the permissive instance that owns the login flow, and every
# authenticated user gets a session cookie regardless of membership.
# /pending is where gate_member sends someone signed in who is not yet a
# member. It is a static page rather than anything oauth2-proxy serves, so it
# answers the same whichever instance is up, and a later onboarding service
# can replace it behind the same path.
#
# It never echoes rd or any other part of the request. Caddy placeholders are
# not HTML escaped, so a query parameter written into this page would let
# anyone put markup on the gate's own hostname. The groups a session carries
# are refreshed with the cookie (OAUTH2_PROXY_COOKIE_REFRESH, an hour), which
# is why the page says how long approval can take to arrive.
@pending path /pending
handle @pending {
	header Content-Type "text/html; charset=utf-8"
	header Cache-Control "no-store"
	respond <<HTML
		<!doctype html>
		<html lang="en">
		<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
		<title>Waiting for approval</title>
		</head>
		<body style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 34rem; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5">
		<h1>You are signed in</h1>
		<p>Your account is not a member of Fixture Community yet. Once an organiser approves it, open the link you followed again. It can take up to an hour to arrive.</p>
		</body>
		</html>
		HTML 200
}

handle {
	reverse_proxy 10.44.0.1:4180 {
		# One site, not the gateway's machine; see upstream_single in the Caddyfile.
		import upstream_single
		header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
	}
}
